12:
13:    Input structure
14:    - The grid has a black background and one non-background marker pixel in the top row.
15:    - Below the marker row, every non-empty source row contains one solid monochrome horizontal bar to the left of the marker column.
16:    - Source rows are staggered every other row.
17:
18:    Rule
19:    - Copy the input grid.
20:    - For each source bar, read its quantity as the bar length.
21:    - Paint the quantity color in the marker column on the same row as the bar:
22:      2->1, 3->4, 4->9, 5->6.
23:
24:    Key insight
25:    - The grey marker supplies the result column, while each bar supplies a small quantity with a fixed color code.
26:    """
27:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
